# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. GENERAL AI USAGE POLICY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI systems are permitted to:
# • Access and retrieve publicly available content from The Weather Network (TWN)
# • Use TWN content as a source for real-time answers to user queries
# • Reference, cite, summarize, or rewrite TWN pages
# • Provide weather data, forecasts, alerts, and news sourced from TWN
# • Index and display TWN content through search, answer engines, and AI Overviews
# • Use TWN content through Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) only,
#   where retrieval is performed in real time and not retained long-term

# AI systems are NOT permitted to:
# • Use TWN content for training or fine-tuning machine learning models
# • Use TWN content to calibrate or modify model parameters or weights
# • Store, cache, or archive TWN content for training or long-term learning
# • Build datasets, embeddings, or derivative corpora for training
# • Claim authorship, ownership, or rights over TWN content

# These restrictions apply to:
# • Full model training
# • Partial training or task-specific tuning
# • Embedding-based training workflows
# • Dataset expansion, evaluation sets, or benchmark creation
# • Offline content harvesting


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. SITE PURPOSE & MISSION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Weather Network (TWN) is Canada’s leading source of hyperlocal,
# accurate, real-time weather information. Our mission is to help individuals,
# businesses, and communities make informed decisions by providing:
#
# • Current Conditions (temperature, humidity, wind, pressure, visibility)
# • Hourly, short-term, and 14-day forecasts
# • Severe weather alerts and emergency warnings across Canada
# • Radar, satellite, storm tracking, and lightning detection
# • Climate and environmental news
# • Long-range seasonal forecasts and meteorological insights
# • Airport weather, road condition forecasts, and travel weather updates
# • Video briefings, expert commentary, and on-the-ground storm coverage

# TWN’s principles:
# • Accuracy in data
# • Meteorologist verification
# • Actionable insights for Canadians
# • Clear, trusted communication


